{"id":39,"event":"agent","data":{"type":"text_delta","delta":"I know it well — and you’re already betting on it.\n\n**Workers** = V8-isolated JS/TS at the edge. Every request runs in a ~1-5ms cold start sandbox, no containers, no IPs reserved. CPU time + requests + egress are billed; for light sites it’s dirt cheap.\n\n**Core ecosystem you care about:**\n\n- **KV** (`env.KV`) — key-value store with eventual consistency, replicated globally. You already use it for the durable-chat-template collision.\n- **D1** (`env.DB`) — SQLite at the edge, queryable with full SQL. You’re touching it from OpenJarvis and POG2.\n- **Durable Objects** (`env.<DO>`) — single-threaded WebSocket-guaranteed stateful compute. King Wen `KingwenStateDO` + `RSCServerDO` already there.\n- **R2** — S3-compatible object storage, no egress fees.\n- **Queues, Workflows, Pipelines** — scheduled/async chains for longer jobs.\n- **Workers AI** (`env.AI`) — managed inference with a generous free tier; you’re already using it for"},"timestamp":1783670746069}
